To write a Fibonacci number function in Rust, you can use a simple recursive approach. Here's an example:

```rust
fn fibonacci(n: u32) -> u32 {
    if n <= 1 {
        n
    } else {
        fibonacci(n - 1) + fibonacci(n - 2)
    }
}

fn main() {
    let n = 10;
    println!("Fibonacci number at position {}: {}", n, fibonacci(n));
}
```

This function calculates the Fibonacci number at a given position `n`. It uses recursion to sum the two preceding numbers until it reaches the base cases.
